Viewer: the music element's own time and duration follow the song; album-art transfers in the log (2026-10-12).

On the car the media card's time and duration were wrong although the box sent the right ones: the page's
music element ran on from the start of the music (0 to 671 s, duration unknown) while the song was at 8 of
269 s, and the card follows that element. The element now goes onto the song's timeline on each new song
and whenever it is more than 3 s off (a seek on the iPhone): the buffered audio (about 0.65 s) is dropped,
the next audio lands at the song position and the duration is the song's. Checked in desktop Chrome: 102.7 s
three seconds after aligning to 100, 7.7 s into the next song, playback continues past the reported end.
Covers are sometimes missing: the box now logs each transfer step and whether the cover reached the page,
and the viewer stats say whether the page has one (art).

